# GridDefence frontend — Vite build-time environment (VITE_* only).
#
# Copy to `frontend/.env` and adjust. Vite reads env from this directory (the
# Vite root); only variables prefixed with `VITE_` are exposed to the browser
# bundle. Do not put secrets here — everything here ships to the client.
#
# See docs/architecture/engineering-map.md for the full basemap / offline model.

# --- Engineering Map basemap styles ------------------------------------------
# DUAL-MODE: these RICH online styles are OPTIONAL. When a configured style
# loads, the map runs in rich mode; when none is set (or one fails), the map
# falls back to a built-in NEUTRAL geographic reference (public-domain Natural
# Earth land/sea/coastline/borders, bundled at frontend/public/map-assets/
# neutral/), which needs no configuration, no internet, and no install. So the
# map works out of the box even with everything below left blank.
#
# Each selectable rich style is a MapLibre **style URL**. A style is offered in
# the UI only when its variable is set; unset styles are omitted (never offered
# and then failing). Availability therefore comes from configuration, not code.
#
# Two operating modes are supported by configuration alone:
#
# 1) Connected mode — an externally hosted rich style (requires internet). Use a
#    governed provider (see docs/engineering/licensing-policy.md §6b). Examples:
#
#    a) OpenFreeMap — no API key, OSM data (ODbL), CORS-enabled, self-hostable.
#       Good for evaluation/dev. Community/donation-hosted: for CRITICAL
#       production, prefer a paid provider (below) or the self-hosted offline
#       package. Allow-list domain: tiles.openfreemap.org
#         VITE_MAP_STYLE_STANDARD=https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty
#
#    b) MapTiler / Stadia — OSM-based, require a DOMAIN-RESTRICTED browser token
#       (create a key restricted to your app origin; a browser token is exposed
#       by design but must be origin-locked — never commit a real value).
#       Allow-list domain: api.maptiler.com (or tiles.stadiamaps.com)
#         VITE_MAP_PROVIDER_TOKEN=your-domain-restricted-key
#         VITE_MAP_STYLE_STANDARD=https://api.maptiler.com/maps/streets-v2/style.json?key=your-domain-restricted-key
#       (Vite has no runtime interpolation — put the key directly in the style
#        URL, or read VITE_MAP_PROVIDER_TOKEN in code if you template the URL.)
#
#       VITE_MAP_STYLE_SATELLITE / VITE_MAP_STYLE_TERRAIN are optional and set
#       the same way when the provider offers them.
#
#    Restart the Vite dev server after changing any VITE_* value (env is read at
#    startup). These are build-time, browser-exposed values — NOT secrets — but
#    still do not commit real provider tokens.
#
# 2) Offline / internal production mode — resources served entirely from the
#    GridDefence deployment (NO internet required). The committed offline
#    Standard package lives under frontend/public/map-assets/standard/ (Phase
#    E.1B, now OPTIONAL): a locally hosted rich basemap. style.json is committed;
#    the .pmtiles archive, glyphs and sprites are fetched by
#    `python scripts/fetch_map_assets.py` (see DEVELOPMENT.md). To use it, point
#    Standard at the local style:
#      VITE_MAP_STYLE_STANDARD=/map-assets/standard/style.json
#    Satellite/Terrain can be added later as their own local packages/URLs:
#      VITE_MAP_STYLE_SATELLITE=/map-assets/satellite/style.json
#      VITE_MAP_STYLE_TERRAIN=/map-assets/terrain/style.json
#
# Left BLANK by default: the map runs in neutral mode out of the box (no rich
# style attempted, no failed request). Set a rich style URL to enable rich mode.
# `VITE_MAP_STYLE_URL` (single-style, pre-E.1A) is still honoured as an alias
# for VITE_MAP_STYLE_STANDARD.
# VITE_MAP_STYLE_STANDARD=
# VITE_MAP_STYLE_SATELLITE=
# VITE_MAP_STYLE_TERRAIN=
